Wonderful AWK command there. For those with hobbies other than AWK, here's what it does: - set variable s to that string: -v s='=== /C=IN/OU=emSign PKI/O=eMudhra Technologies Limited/CN=emSign ECC Root CA - G3'
- on lines matching the regex between //, set skip to false: /^(===|###) /{skip=0}
- on lines matching s, set skip to true: $0==s{skip=1}
- if skip is false, print the line: !skip
